From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:42:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Give the layer of a canvas its colour description through
 colour management

A canvas that has a native surface of its own under a compositor with
colour management gets a KisCanvasSurfaceColorSpaceManager on that
window, which sets the image description of the surface for the mode
the user chose (Preferred, Rec. 709 gamma 2.2 or linear, Rec. 2020 PQ)
and reports back the display config the canvas is rendered for. A
canvas of a session that started for stereo is shown through a layer,
whose surface is the canvas's own and had none, so KWin took it to be
sRGB and Krita took the canvas to be limited to sRGB.

The canvas hands the window of the layer it shows through to
KisCanvas2::attachSurfaceColorManager, the code that the native
surface used, as the layer becomes ready, and again when the canvas
changes between the layer of a stereo pair and the one of a normal
document. The "limited to sRGB" warning is no longer given for a
canvas that will be shown through a layer.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
